    {
      "id": "2110711793337135550",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-10-15T12:38:01.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-15 20:38:01",
      "type": "引用",
      "type_label": "引用",
      "text": "The whole world will watch this",
      "quote": {
        "author": "Teslaconomics",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1882967991362727936/bySD-Rwj_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-15 02:51:46",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-10-14T18:51:46.000Z",
        "id": "2110443463821185532",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUnNIVla8AAWqXh.jpg?name=small"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "height": 1024,
            "type": "photo",
            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUnNIVla8AAWqXh.jpg?name=small",
            "width": 1536
          }
        ],
        "name": "Teslaconomics",
        "text": "The only other person who’s ever made me this excited about a product unveil was Steve Jobs. Watching him introduce the first iPhone is a huge part of why I fell in love with technology.\n\nElon brings that feeling back for me, but honestly, I think he takes it to a whole different level. Tomorrow, he and the Tesla team are unveiling the next-gen Roadster, and I seriously cannot wait. \n\nThe Roadster they showed in 2017 already promised 0–60 mph in 1.9 seconds. Since then, Elon has talked about a Tesla–SpaceX collaboration, having it fly, and getting that time below ONE second, and calling it “the least interesting part” of the car. \n\nHow do you say something like that and expect me NOT to be excited?!\n\nBut beyond how fast it goes, I want to see something that makes me sit there and say, “Wow… how in the world did they build that?” I honestly don’t know what they’re going to show us, and that’s part of what makes this so much fun. I really want to be surprised and see the unthinkable.\n\nThese days I feel many older people don’t get that excited about things… I only see that spark in kids. But imo, we should still get excited about people building cool things. We should still root for the nerds, engineers, and designers trying to do something that has never been done before.\n\nAnd I hope there’s a kid watching tomorrow who feels what I felt watching Steve Jobs introduce the iPhone. Someone who sees this car and starts wondering how it works, sketching their own ideas, or thinking about what they could build someday.\n\nI hope y’all are ready to have your minds blown. \n\nI’m rooting for you, Elon, and the entire Tesla team behind this car. \n\nGo give us a night we’ll never forget!",
        "url": "https://x.com/Teslaconomics/status/2110443463821185532",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": null,
      "reply_to": "",
